## Step 0: Decide the parent

Do this before writing any code, and record the result. It goes into the Step 1 PR description and the final report.

### 0.1 Find the resource name pattern

Look up the `google.api.resource` annotation on `{PROTO_MESSAGE}`.

- The protos are under `.build/third_party/googleapis/google/...`, after `dev/tools/controllerbuilder/generate-proto.sh` has run; `generate.sh` runs it for you.
- Alternatively, run `grep -i {PROTO_MESSAGE} docs/ai/metadata/cloudassetinventory_names.jsonl`.

The parent pattern is the name pattern without its last `/{collection}/{id}` pair. For example, `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/exampleStores/{example_store}` has the parent `projects/{project}/locations/{location}`.

### 0.2 Pick the `ParentRef` type

| Parent pattern | `ParentRef` Go type | YAML in `create.yaml` |
|---|---|---|
| `projects/{project}` | `*refsv1beta1.ProjectRef` | `parentRef: {external: projects/${projectId}}` |
| `projects/{project}/locations/{location}` | `*parent.ProjectAndLocationRef` | `parentRef: {projectRef: {external: projects/${projectId}}, location: us-central1}` |
| `folders/{folder}` | `*refs.FolderRef` (from `apis/refs`) | `parentRef: {external: folders/123}` |
| `organizations/{organization}` | `*refsv1beta1.OrganizationRef` | `parentRef: {external: organizations/123}` |
| Ends in another resource, e.g. `.../workstationConfigs/{config}` | That kind's `*{ParentKind}Ref` | `parentRef: {name: <parent object name>}` |

### 0.3 Stop and report instead of improvising if:

- **More than one parent kind.** The resource has several name patterns with different parents (for example project, folder and organization). The shared multi-kind reference type doesn't exist yet.
- **Parent pattern not in the table.** For example `organizations/{o}/locations/{l}`, `folders/{f}/locations/{l}`, `projects/{p}/regions/{r}`, `projects/{p}/zones/{z}` or `projects/{p}/global`. No shared type exists for these yet.
- **Parent kind not in KCC.** The parent is another resource that KCC doesn't support yet. That kind needs to be implemented first.

### 0.4 Check the parent side (resource parents only)

Open `apis/{parentGroup}/{version}/{parentkind}_reference.go` and `_identity.go`. The parent kind must provide:

- a `{ParentKind}Ref` with `External`, `Name` and `Namespace`, implementing `refsv1beta1.ExternalRef` (which includes `ParseExternalToIdentity`);
- a `{ParentKind}Identity` built with `gcpurls.Template`.

If a piece is missing (for example, `GKEHubScopeRef` has no `ParseExternalToIdentity`), add it in the parent's package as part of Step 1 and say so in the PR. Don't change the parent's CRD schema.

